{"name":"Pasha Brown","hex":"#c3b7a4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pasha","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A high-ranking Turkish military officer, especially as a commander or regional governor; the highest honorary title during the Ottoman Empire.","The Indian butterfly Herona marathus, family Nymphalidae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pasha"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pasha","blocks":[{"text":"Pasha was a high-rank, aristocratic title in the Ottoman political and military system, typically granted by the Sultan to governors, generals, dignitaries, and others carrying the tughra. Pasha, in one of its various ranks, is equivalent to the British title of Lord. Pasha was one of the highest titles in the 20th-century Kingdom of Egypt and it was also used in Morocco in the 20th century, where it denoted a regional official or governor of a district."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pasha","wikidata":"Q184951"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Ottoman_tui_1877_romanian_capture.jpg/500px-Ottoman_tui_1877_romanian_capture.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c